Z||000004||loafer87gt||01-25-2000||01:30 PM||||Bring on the global warming!! Maybe then things will actually get above 0 for more than 5 months a year up here in Northern Saskatchewan. Things are finally warming up here, by Friday its supposed to get around -2!! This is really odd as it usually around -30-35 this time of year. Bizarre. One interesting bit though, my Fiero is the best winter vehicle I have ever driven. I got a set of Canadian Tire snow tires and she plows through anything. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||01-25-2000||03:35 PM||||I love global warming!  Here in Minnesota up until jan. 10 we had about 10" total of snow fall.  You could drive around and actually see grass... Of course, it's gotten a little worse now.  Oh well, only makes it easier to whip shitties.  <BR>bHooper -- what's wrong with being like "<B>freaking Minnesota</B>"!?!?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierosound||01-25-2000||03:36 PM||||Bhooper..<P>Looks like you got quite a dump of snow.  We haven't gotten any more than 4 inches total this winter here in Calgary, Canada.  If the Winter Olympics were here this year, we'd have to truck in snow from the mountain ski resorts!!!  We could still get a spring snowstorm though - and that could easily equal an entire winter's worth of snow in a couple of days.  Haven't seen one like that in four years either!!<P>Calgary Webcams - <A HREF="http://www.cict.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cict.com/</A> <P>Have fun   it's all temporary!!  <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||7
